.TH HD-BACKUP-VM 8 "October 2026" "hd-backup" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-backup-vm \- back up a virtual machine on ZFS volumes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-backup-vm
.I vm dir owner
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-backup-vm
backs up the libvirt virtual machine
.I vm
to the folder
.IR dir / vm .
All disks of the VM must be ZFS volumes; a VM with other disks, like image
files, is refused.
CD-ROM and floppy drives are left out.
Run it as root.
.PP
A run:
.IP 1. 4
dumps the XML of the VM and copies its NVRAM when it boots with UEFI;
.IP 2. 4
freezes the filesystems of a running guest with the QEMU guest agent;
without the agent, the snapshot is crash-consistent.
A VM that is shut off is not frozen: its disks are consistent as they are.
A VM in another state, like paused, is not frozen either, and its snapshot
is crash-consistent;
.IP 3. 4
takes a snapshot
.BI backup\- YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS
of every disk, atomically per pool, and thaws a frozen guest;
.IP 4. 4
writes a ZFS stream of every disk through
.BR zstd (1):
a full stream for a disk without earlier streams, otherwise an incremental
one from the snapshot of the last backup;
.IP 5. 4
records the next sequence number and the new snapshot, destroys the older
backup snapshots, and gives all files of the backup to
.IR owner .
.PP
When a run does not finish, the guest is thawed, and the snapshots and files
of the run are removed again, so the next run continues from the last backup
that did finish.
Only one backup of a VM runs at a time.
.PP
When the snapshot of the last backup is gone, the backup cannot be continued:
move the backup folder away, and the next run starts again with full
streams.
.SH FILES
In
.IR dir / vm :
.TP
.IB vm .xml
The XML of the VM at the last finished backup.
.TP
.IB vm _VARS.fd
Its NVRAM, for a VM that boots with UEFI.
.TP
.IB dataset . NNNN .zst
The streams of a disk, with the slashes of the dataset replaced by
underscores, numbered from 0000.
Restore them in order, see
.BR hd\-restore\-vm (8).
.TP
.IB vm .sequence
The next sequence number and the snapshot of the last backup.
.PP
.TP
.IR /run/lock/hd\-backup\-vm\- vm .lock
The lock of a running backup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the backup finished, 1 on an error, 2 on wrong arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd\-backup\-vms (8),
.BR hd\-restore\-vm (8),
.BR virsh (1),
.BR zfs (8)
